/**
 * JPA persistence: one entity per table and one Spring Data JPA repository per entity.
 *
 * <p>The schema is owned by Flyway ({@code backend/db}); Hibernate only validates it ({@code ddl-auto=validate}).
 * Ids are UUIDs generated by Hibernate, timestamps are set in {@code @PrePersist} (UTC), and every user-owned row is
 * scoped by {@code userId} (the Keycloak subject, see {@code CurrentUser}). The few PostgreSQL-specific statements
 * that JPQL cannot express (idempotent {@code INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING} used when provisioning users) are
 * native {@code @Query} methods on the repositories.
 */
